.git

# Every .env shape, template included: nothing inside an image reads a
# template, and `.env` alone would have baked a `.env.production` or
# `.env.staging` sitting in a developer's checkout into an image layer.
.env*

env/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.claude/
.superpowers/
.remember/
docs/

# AI-team config: no image stage reads either, and in dev the `.:/app` bind
# mount supplies them from the host anyway.
CLAUDE.md
.mcp.json
node_modules/

# Machine-local compose overrides never belong in an image.
compose.override.y*ml
docker-compose.override.y*ml
